# Every guard in this repository is a command someone has to choose to run.
# This hook makes that choice for them: no commit lands without the pin check,
# the layer rule, the NFR23 literal sweep and the accessibility assertions
# having passed. A guard nobody runs is a guard nobody has.
#
# `npm run build` is deliberately not here. It is the only one of the four
# checks with a side effect — it rewrites `out/`, which `npm run dev` is
# serving from, so a commit made during a dev session would clobber the running
# app's bundles. It is also the check that grows with the renderer while the
# other three stay flat, so it is the one that would eventually make this hook
# something people reach for `--no-verify` to escape. `npm run package` builds
# before it ships anything; a commit does not need to.
#
# Escape hatch, for the record: `git commit --no-verify` skips this. That is a
# deliberate, visible act, which is the point.

npm run lint
npm run typecheck
npm test
